# arc42 documentation prose — DO NOT auto-format.
#
# Prettier's markdown printer rewrites emphasis delimiters, and this repo's
# docs are dense with bare snake_case identifiers in prose (RTC_NOINIT,
# hb_failure, capture_gate, date_trunc, module_configs, …). Underscores in
# adjacent identifiers get paired as an emphasis span, so a reformat silently
# turned `RTC_NOINIT survives … a _successful_ upload` into
# `RTC*NOINIT survives … a \_successful* upload` — the identifier destroyed and
# ungreppable, the paragraph rendered as one italic run. Caught in PR #193
# only because a reviewer diffed an unrelated chapter.
#
# Lesson: docs/11-risks-and-technical-debt/README.md → "A markdown formatter
# rewrites emphasis, and this repo writes identifiers in prose".
docs/**/*.md
